Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","02.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":233,"path":234,"stem":235,"icon":236},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","02.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":238,"title":205,"body":239,"description":1205,"extension":1206,"links":1207,"meta":1208,"navigation":1209,"path":206,"seo":1210,"stem":207,"__hash__":1211},"docs\u002F02.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":240,"value":241,"toc":1188},"minimark",[242,246,250,254,265,272,276,286,292,296,301,304,343,347,354,361,367,371,378,433,443,456,520,523,591,594,598,601,607,611,614,620,624,627,633,637,644,884,888,894,1095,1099,1184],[243,244,25],"h2",{"id":245},"overview",[247,248,249],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[243,251,253],{"id":252},"format","Format",[255,256,261],"pre",{"className":257,"code":259,"language":260},[258],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[262,263,259],"code",{"__ignoreMap":264},"",[247,266,267,268,271],{},"Everything in brackets (",[262,269,270],{},"[]",") is optional.",[243,273,275],{"id":274},"case","Case",[247,277,278,279,282,283,285],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[262,280,281],{},"OrderService"," and ",[262,284,281],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[255,287,290],{"className":288,"code":289,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[262,291,289],{"__ignoreMap":264},[243,293,295],{"id":294},"components","Components",[297,298,300],"h3",{"id":299},"scheme","Scheme",[247,302,303],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[305,306,307,319],"table",{},[308,309,310],"thead",{},[311,312,313,316],"tr",{},[314,315,300],"th",{},[314,317,318],{},"Description",[320,321,322,333],"tbody",{},[311,323,324,330],{},[325,326,327],"td",{},[262,328,329],{},"srv",[325,331,332],{},"Published services and their methods",[311,334,335,340],{},[325,336,337],{},[262,338,339],{},"stream",[325,341,342],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[297,344,346],{"id":345},"scope","Scope",[247,348,349,350,353],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[262,351,352],{},"@"," symbol.",[247,355,356,357,360],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[262,358,359],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[255,362,365],{"className":363,"code":364,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[262,366,364],{"__ignoreMap":264},[297,368,370],{"id":369},"zone","Zone",[247,372,373,374,377],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[262,375,376],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[305,379,380,388],{},[308,381,382],{},[311,383,384,386],{},[314,385,370],{},[314,387,318],{},[320,389,390,403,413,423],{},[311,391,392,397],{},[325,393,394],{},[262,395,396],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[325,398,399,400,360],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[262,401,402],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[311,404,405,410],{},[325,406,407],{},[262,408,409],{},"app-api",[325,411,412],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[311,414,415,420],{},[325,416,417],{},[262,418,419],{},"management-api",[325,421,422],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[311,424,425,430],{},[325,426,427],{},[262,428,429],{},"system-api",[325,431,432],{},"Platform-internal services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[247,434,435,436,439,440,442],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[262,437,438],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[262,441,429],{}," is rejected.",[247,444,445,446,448,449,452,453,455],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[262,447,402],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[262,450,451],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[262,454,376],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[305,457,458,471],{},[308,459,460],{},[311,461,462,465,468],{},[314,463,464],{},"Participant",[314,466,467],{},"May send to",[314,469,470],{},"May subscribe to",[320,472,473,489,508],{},[311,474,475,478,486],{},[325,476,477],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[325,479,480,482,483],{},[262,481,409],{},", ",[262,484,485],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[325,487,488],{},"reply destinations only",[311,490,491,494,503],{},[325,492,493],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[325,495,496,482,498,482,500],{},[262,497,419],{},[262,499,409],{},[262,501,502],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[325,504,505,507],{},[262,506,502],{}," — its applications' zones",[311,509,510,513,516],{},[325,511,512],{},"SYSTEM",[325,514,515],{},"everything",[325,517,518],{},[262,519,429],{},[247,521,522],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[305,524,525,538],{},[308,526,527],{},[311,528,529,532,535],{},[314,530,531],{},"Server",[314,533,534],{},"Hosts",[314,536,537],{},"Reaches",[320,539,540,557,574],{},[311,541,542,545,549],{},[325,543,544],{},"org",[325,546,547],{},[262,548,419],{},[325,550,551,482,553,482,555],{},[262,552,419],{},[262,554,429],{},[262,556,409],{},[311,558,559,562,568],{},[325,560,561],{},"system",[325,563,564,482,566],{},[262,565,429],{},[262,567,419],{},[325,569,570,482,572],{},[262,571,429],{},[262,573,419],{},[311,575,576,578,585],{},[325,577,438],{},[325,579,580,482,582],{},[262,581,409],{},[262,583,584],{},"app.*",[325,586,587,482,589],{},[262,588,409],{},[262,590,584],{},[247,592,593],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[297,595,597],{"id":596},"resource-name","Resource Name",[247,599,600],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[255,602,605],{"className":603,"code":604,"language":260},[258],"srv:\u002F\